            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent spontaneous coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>566-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recurrence of spontaneous coronary artery dissection is a rare event with limited documentation of its existence in the world's literature. We present a case of recurrent spontaneous coronary artery dissection treated with coronary artery bypass surgery and discuss the literature regarding this entity.</AbstractText>
